\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.12}{\ignorespaces Predictions with standard errors for fixed effects in a generalized additive model with splines for ratio by comparison and ratio by display method. It is clear that the separated comparisons are easier to estimate when small, right around 50\%, or large, and harder to estimate between these points. What is interesting is that no such trend is present for adjacent comparisons.\relax }}{44}{figure.caption.33}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-gam-pred-chart}{{3.12}{44}{Predictions with standard errors for fixed effects in a generalized additive model with splines for ratio by comparison and ratio by display method. It is clear that the separated comparisons are easier to estimate when small, right around 50\%, or large, and harder to estimate between these points. What is interesting is that no such trend is present for adjacent comparisons.\relax }{figure.caption.33}{}}
